\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Ideal graph fragment showing a phi node merging two additions}
\label{fig:ideal-graph}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Peephole Optimization in JITs}\label{sec:jit-peephole}

JIT compilers use peephole optimizations extensively because they are fast and effective:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Algebraic simplification}: $x + 0 \to x$, $x \times 1 \to x$, $x \times 0 \to 0$.
  \item \textbf{Strength reduction}: $x \times 2^n \to x \ll n$.
  \item \textbf{Null check elimination}: if a value is proven non-null by a dominating guard, remove redundant null checks.
  \item \textbf{Bounds check elimination}: if an index is proven in-bounds by a dominating check, remove redundant bounds checks.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}\label{sec:jit-summary}

JIT compilation is the cornerstone of performance for dynamic and managed language implementations. By observing actual program behavior and specializing code accordingly, JIT compilers achieve performance that rivals or exceeds ahead-of-time compilation for many workloads. The key techniques---tiered compilation, inline caching, speculative optimization with guards, on-stack replacement, and deoptimization---form a coherent architecture that balances startup time, steady-state performance, and adaptability.

\begin{historical}
JIT compilation has its roots in the early days of Java. Sun's original JVM (1996) used a pure interpreter. The HotSpot VM (1999) introduced adaptive compilation, selecting methods for compilation based on profiling data. The concept of tiered compilation evolved through the 2000s and 2010s, with HotSpot eventually adopting a five-tier system. JavaScript JITs evolved rapidly in the late 2000s: V8's introduction of hidden classes and inline caching (2008) revolutionized JavaScript performance. The concept of on-stack replacement, pioneered by the Self VM (1994), is now standard in all serious JIT compilers. Modern JITs like GraalVM and V8's TurboFan represent the state of the art, using sophisticated IRs and speculative optimization to achieve remarkable performance.
\end{historical}
